WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.410
Sikhs believe God is
timeless and formless:

2
00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:06.120
beyond anything the mind can grasp.

3
00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:08.820
The scripture's first
symbol says it plainly:

4
00:00:08.870 --> 00:00:11.190
one God, with no second.

5
00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:12.840
Ik Onkar.

6
00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:15.560
Yet Sikh hymns speak to God as you.

7
00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:19.560
They call God a friend, a
beloved, and the True King.

8
00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:22.670
So can a God without
qualities also be a friend,

9
00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:24.520
a mother and a king?

10
00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:27.600
In this mission, you'll
unpack the Ik Onkar symbol,

11
00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:29.700
and what each part of it means to Sikhs.

12
00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:33.490
Then you'll build a web of
the ways Sikhs describe God:

13
00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:37.670
creator, sustainer,
all-powerful, all-knowing.

14
00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:42.560
Your mission: find out how Sikhs can
call a God without qualities a friend,

15
00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:44.040
a mother and a king.
